usercontent.com/u/87827018?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack","html_url":"https://github.com/voxelstack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voxelstack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:44:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T18:03:12Z","body":"Putting a bit more thought into this: a `.gdshader` file only contains the shader source, making me think it's not possible to have any extra properties defined on a resource that inherits from it being properly saved to disk.\n\nSo I guess what I am trying to do is simply not possible and my only option is to have a resource that stores extra properties and also owns a shader, using the Shader's changed event to react to source code changes?\n\nThe reason I didn't want to do it this way is inconvenience of dealing with the extra resource that I cannot assign to properties of type Shader.\n\nIn a way related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/84653","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6174596033/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]